# why: go:embed copies the checkout byte for byte, so the pi extension and OpenCode plugin pitwall writes must not turn CRLF on Windows.
*.ts text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
# why: the same for the skill: a CRLF copy is not the file a release wrote, so IsSkill takes an unedited install for an edited one and never refreshes it.
internal/agent/pitwall_skill.md text eol=lf
# why: the binary embeds this script and pipes it to sh on a host, which reads a CRLF line end as part of the command.
scripts/get-host.sh text eol=lf
# why: Windows checkouts turn LF into CRLF, and golden files compare byte for byte.
**/testdata/** -text
# why: go:embed renders these into the Homebrew, Scoop and AUR files, which are LF like their goldens.
scripts/pkgrender/tmpl/** text eol=lf
